  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Why does Russia own land between Poland and Lithuania?",
      "scene": 0,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K1",
        "K2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It is Kaliningrad, on the Baltic Sea.",
      "scene": 1,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Until 1946, it was a German city called Königsberg.",
      "scene": 2,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Teutonic Knights founded it in 1255.",
      "scene": 3,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1701, a king was crowned in its castle.",
      "scene": 4,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1944, British bombs burned its old centre.",
      "scene": 6,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On 9 April 1945, the Soviets captured it.",
      "scene": 7,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Potsdam, the Allies agreed, in principle, to give it to the Soviets.",
      "scene": 8,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Renamed Kaliningrad after Mikhail Kalinin, who was unrelated to it.",
      "scene": 9,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Every land link to Russia now crosses NATO and EU.",
      "scene": 10,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A German city became Russian.",
      "scene": 11,
      "claim_ids": [
        "K12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The full story is on our channel.",
